1	//! A machine that runs an IMASM module. Dispatch is on the glyph and nothing
2	//! else; what an instruction *was* in x86 survives only as payload the glyph
3	//! reads. Ported from imasm_vm.py. ⊞ engages the ALU, ⋈ links slots, ⊡ commits
4	//! to memory, ⊤ makes a truth and ⊥ consumes one, ∈ splits and ∋ fuses, > calls
5	//! and ⊣ terminates, < transfers, ⊙ transfers through data.
