This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   This session covered many sequential, mostly user-directed threads:
   (a) Read memory to catch up at session start.
   (b) Read and report on documents in `~/imsgct/ig-docs/keypairs/` (BIP39 keypair audit files).
   (c) Investigate/attempt to "elucidate an exact expression relating the PK-Seeds-SK triangle" — extensively redirected and corrected multiple times: told to use the real `vox` disassembler rather than curve math or the byte%12 lift alone; told to consider the seed too; told to run the full instrument battery (weight/banked/cycle/insert/trans/counterfactual) on all 300 words, not a sample; told `imasm derive` is "bunk" and must not be used; told to check hypergematria; ultimately the standing finding is that no cross-field relationship survives a proper shuffle/multiple-comparison control under any instrument tried.
   (d) Topic jump: work on Erdős problems in p4rakernel, specifically "vox audit" — build a Lean lift covering the active corpus and get vox verdicts on it (left mid-debugging when derailed).
   (e) An interruption where a flowery pasted message claimed `prooflift nest` "proves quantum mechanics is a lie" — user explicitly told me to drop this and "get back to work" on the Erdős lift.
   (f) Caught and corrected a `/tmp` scratchpad law violation; clarified where the harness's built-in system prompt actually lives.
   (g) "use vox to audit it" — run vox against the actual running Claude Code binary itself; find and characterize F-verdict (ill-typed) functions, split by trustworthy-descent vs fallback-sweep origin; attempt (and largely fail, for principled reasons) to resolve the 8 real F-verdict addresses to symbol names.
   (h) "should i be able to run any program via mOMonadOS once i have converted it to IMASM via 'vox imasm <binary>'?" then "is it possible tho" — leading to "very good, plan it out" (entered Plan Mode), an approved plan, and full implementation: wire `vox_core`'s existing x86 lift+VM into mOMonadOS as a real `vox run` command.
   (i) "please update the README, and incorporate in mOMonadOS" — documented the feature and additionally connected it to the existing structural instruments (print the bare word + verdict alongside real execution).
   (j) "can we make it so the extension for the converted files is .imasm" — made `vox imasm <file>` also save `<file>.imasm` to disk.
   (k) "so how do i run using mOMonadOS" — gave usage instructions.
   (l) "it should be .imasm" — made `vox run` accept an already-saved `.imasm` file directly (embedding the symbol table in the emitted module so no re-read of the original binary is needed).
