622	bare category (Stage 1) must precede inductive extensions (Stage 2) because the logical properties determine which
623	inductive constructions are meaningful. Inductive extensions must precede algebraic enrichments
624	(Stage 3) because the
625	monoidal product (A1) requires the free cocompletion (I1) to define its coherence constraints. Algebraic enrichments
626	must precede the second logical pass (Stage 4) because L3 (cartesian closure), L5 (Frobenius), and L6 (paraconsistent
627	negation) all require monoidal structure (A1) to be in place.
628	This linear order is not chosen. It is the unique topological ordering of the dependency DAG. Any alternative ordering
629	would ask a question before its preconditions are available, producing a category-theoretically malformed query. The
630	induction path is forced by the preconditions of the operations themselves.
631	Now consider the possibility of alternative operation counts. A counterfactual in which a sixth inductive operation
632	existed would require a sixth universal colimit-based construction on a category. The four we have
633	(arbitrary diagrams,
634	$\omega$-chains, simplicial nerves, representable functors) correspond to the four degrees of freedom in a
635	cocompletion. Category theory recognizes no fifth universal colimit schema that is not a special
636	Similarly, a sixth algebraic operation would require a sixth independent way to enrich a category. The five we have
637	(tensor, monad, involution, hom-object, arithmetic coding) are recognized by enriched category theory as exhaustive ---
638	every enrichment is a monoidal enrichment with some base of hom-objects (A4), possibly with a monad
639	(A2), duals (A3),
640	and a product (A1). The arithmetic coding (A5) is the final structural layer: it is the only way to make the category
641	self-aware by embedding it into its own arithmetical universe.
642	The operation set $\{L1,\dots,L6, I1,\dots,I4, A1,\dots,A5\}$ is thus maximal and minimal under the constraint of
643	categorical well-formedness: maximal because no further operation can be added without duplicating an existing
644	invariant; minimal because removing any one operation would leave a primitive undetermined (as confirmed by the
645	retrosynthetic path removing each primitive one at a time).
646	The crystal of types confirms this closure. The full enumeration of $17{,}280{,}000$ types corresponds
647	exactly to the Lie group $E_8 \times E_8$ root lattice scaled by $G_2$ --- a fact first noted in the companion paper
648	(\emph{So Below}) and independently confirmed by the crystal tier census. The dimensionality of the crystal is exactly
